🟢 Restaurant Booking System — REQUIREMENTS (Amazon SDE-2 Style)
0️⃣ How Amazon expects you to start (say this aloud)

“I’ll first clarify functional requirements and scope the problem before designing.”

That sentence itself is a positive signal.

1️⃣ Functional Requirements (CORE)

These are the must-have features. Say them clearly.

Booking related

User should be able to search restaurants

User should be able to view restaurant details

User should be able to check table availability for a given date & time

User should be able to make a reservation

User should be able to cancel a reservation

System should prevent double booking of tables

Restaurant / Table related

A restaurant has multiple tables

Tables have capacity (number of seats)

Booking is made for:

date

time slot

number of guests

Constraints (important)

A booking is valid for a fixed duration (e.g., 1 or 2 hours)

Restaurant can choose operating hours

Booking should only be allowed during operating hours

2️⃣ Non-Functional Requirements (keep light)

Only mention these briefly:

System should handle concurrent bookings

System should be consistent (no double bookings)

Read-heavy system (search & availability)

⚠️ Do NOT talk about scalability, sharding, microservices unless asked.

3️⃣ What is OUT OF SCOPE (say this explicitly)

This is very important in Amazon interviews.

“I’ll keep the following out of scope unless required:”

Payments

Reviews & ratings

Waitlist

Notifications (SMS/email)

Dynamic pricing

Recommendation engine

🧠 Interviewer thought:

“Candidate can control scope.”

4️⃣ Clarifying Questions (ask 2–3 max)

Ask these before design:

Is booking always table-based, or can we auto-assign tables?

Is booking per table or per restaurant (any table)?

Is overlapping booking allowed if capacity permits?

Usually interviewer says:

“Assume table-based booking, auto-assignment allowed.”

5️⃣ Fixed assumptions (state them clearly)

If interviewer doesn’t answer everything, say:

Booking duration = 2 hours

One booking → one table

One user can have multiple bookings

Time slots are fixed (e.g., 6–8, 8–10)

These assumptions are perfectly acceptable.

6️⃣ What interviewer EXPECTS next (important)

After requirements, interviewer expects you to:

List core entities

Add attributes with proper data types

Define APIs

Design DB schema

Implement one core flow (e.g., create booking)

We’ll do that step by step.

